:: Bog Cult Salem Read Book
<<npc Salem>><<person1>>
You sit next to Salem, respecting <<his>> space, and begin to read from one of his religious books.
<br><br>
"There are many theories related to the origin and proper worship of the Dark Mother; some say she is the daughter of Auriga, others say she's a godly aspect of Auriga, and even others say they are one and the same. These claims are born from the similar nature of the two deities, though the truth is that it may simply be unknowable."
<br><br>
Salem sits alert and listens as you read the religious script. <<His>> eyes follow your finger as you read the page. After a little bit, you close the book and sit up. Salem looks to you and speaks. "Done already? Typically my study sessions tend to go on a bit longer, but I am okay with calling it here. U-um... thank you. This was nice."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Story
<<npc Salem>><<person1>>
You sit next to Salem, respecting <<his>> space, and begin to tell your own story.
<br><br>
<<if $english gte 600>>
    You begin to tell a story similar to the stories you have studied in school or the library. Something engaging but grounded. A typical hero's journey. You can tell it's not something Salem is used to hearing. 
    <br><br>
    <<He>> falls silent as you tell your story. <<He>> remains silent and leans in intently, not realizing how close <<he>> has gotten. As you wrap up the story, Salem notices how intently <<he>> was listening and pulls back a little. 
    <br><br>
    "Oh, um, sorry, I didn't realize I had gotten so close... It's just, I have never heard such a story before. T-thank you, this was really nice. M-maybe we can do this again sometime soon?"
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><<npcincr Salem love 3>><<endevent>><</link>><<gglove>>
<<else>>
    You begin to tell a story but begin to get lost along the way. The story is full of inconsistencies, and the characters behave strangely. As you speak, Salem tilts <<his>> head a bit, confused. 
    <br><br>
    "So w-wait. This is something you're just making up on the spot?" <<He>> thinks for a moment. "It's impressive but... w-why would the characters act like that? It doesn't really... make sense?" 
    <br><br>
    Salem catches <<himself>> and turns away, looking down. "S-sorry, I didn't mean to sound so ungrateful. Thank you for this."
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

