:: Salem Arcade
    <<npc Salem>><<person1>>
    As you and Salem make your way into town, <<he>> begins to slightly hide behind you. You let <<him>> trail slightly as you pass the hospital. <<He>> peers at the injured people with interest as you continue down Oxford and finally arrive on Starfish Street. You open the arcade door, are hit with cool air conditioning, and walk in with Salem right behind.
    <br><br>
    <<if $salemarcade is 1>>
        As you enter, Salem has already began to relax, away from prying eyes. <<He>> slowly lets go of your arm and looks at the arcade cabinets. Without waiting for your input, <<he>> pulls you toward a newer one. "Hey look at this one." <<He>> smiles warmly at you. "Do you want to try playing with me? I have been practicing in my head for this moment."
        <br><br>
        You and Salem spend some time playing games together. <<He>> is still pretty bad at games but you are surprised to see <<him>> manage to take a game off you. As <<he>> catches sight of the clock, <<his>> face sinks a little. "I-is it already that time?" <<He>> looks worried. "S-sorry I have to get back to the Fellowship before my duties."
        <br><br>
        Salem reaches out <<his>> hand to take yours as the two of you return down the path back to the Fellowship, sneaking Salem back to <<his>> room and closing the door gently.
        <br><br>
        <<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
    <<else>>
        The arcade is mostly empty which causes Salem to relax. <<He>> slowly lets go of your arm and looks at the arcade cabinets. Curiously Salem touches one and tilts <<his>> head. "What are these things? Are they kind of like a television?" You take a moment to explain what an arcade is and Salem looks dumbfounded. "W-wait so it's like a television that you control what happens on the glass? That's so cool!"
        <br><br>
        You and Salem spend some time playing games together after you teach <<him>> the controls. <<He>> pretty quickly learns but not enough to actually win anything. Despite this, <<he>> seems to be having fun. "I-is it already that time?" <<He>> looks worried. "S-sorry I have to get back to the Fellowship before my duties."
        <br><br>
        Salem reaches out <<his>> hand to take yours as the two of you return down the path back to the Fellowship, sneaking Salem back to <<his>> room and closing the door gently.
        <br><br>
        <<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><<set $salemarcade to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
    <</if>>

:: Salem Museum
<<npc Salem>><<person1>>
    As you and Salem make your way into town, <<he>> begins to slightly hide behind you. You let <<him>> trail slightly as you arrive on Wolf Street. <<He>> casts nervous glances toward the church and hurries to get to the next street. As you arrive at Oxford Street, you open the museum and walk in with Salem right behind.
    <br><br>
    <<if $museumintro is 1 and $salemwintermeet is undefined>>
        <<npc Winter 2>><<person2>>
        As you enter the museum, you catch sight of Winter with a group of visitors. You approach and Winter turns to face you. "Oh it's you, and I see you brought someone else here?" Winter lowers <<his>> eyes to look at Salem. "Just tell your little friend not to touch anything." Winter returns <<his>> attention to the visitors, leaving you and Salem alone.
        <br><br>
        Salem turns to you with wide eyes. <<person1>>"W-who was that, <<he>> was scary." Salem continues to hide behind you, peeking out at Winter from across the room. The two of you look through the museum's exhibits. 
        <br><br>
        <<link [[Next|Salem Museum 2]]>><</link>>
    <<elseif $museumintro is 1 and $salemwintermeet is 1>>
        As you enter the museum Winter catches sight and approaches you and Salem once again. "I see the two of you are back. Remember, no touching the antiques and stay where you belong." As Winter turns back to the visitors, Salem turns to whisper to you.
        <br><br>
        "T-there's something I saw last time that I want you to see." Salem makes sure Winter is not looking before <<he>> leads you back into a side room of the museum you have never really seen before. "Y-you remember how I told you the Fellowship had some trinkets like this?" <<He>> reveals a small black altar.
        <br><br>
        "We have something just like this back at the church. It's an altar to the Dark Mother. I wonder where they got this one." Salem spends some time explaining the Fellowship's method of ritualistic worship before you hear footsteps outside the room.
        <br><br>
        <<link [[Next|Salem Museum 2]]>><</link>>
    <<elseif $salemmuseum is 1>>
        As you enter the museum, Salem pulls you to the side. "T-there's something I saw last time that I want you to see." Salem leads you back into a side room of the museum you have never really seen before. "Y-you remember how I told you the Fellowship had some trinkets like this?" <<He>> reveals a small black altar.
        <br><br>
        "We have something just like this back at the church. It's an altar to the Dark Mother. I wonder where they got this one." Salem spends some time explaining the Fellowship's method of ritualistic worship before you hear footsteps outside the room.
        <br><br>
        <<link [[Next|Salem Museum 2]]>><</link>>
    <<else>>
        As you enter the museum, you catch sight of a guide with a group of visitors. Not really seeing the need for a guide at this time, the two of you look through the museum's exhibits. 
        <br><br>
        Salem stops to look at a couple things with intrigue. "Y-you know, the Fellowship actually has some really old trinkets just like this. M-maybe someday I could show you some. I-if you're interested anyway."
        <br><br>
        <<link [[Next|Salem Museum 2]]>><</link>>
    <</if>>

